    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n47599" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">taxus</span></b> , i, f., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a yew</i>, <i>yew-tree.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 16,
				10, 20, § 50</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Caes. B. G.
				6, 31</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Verg. E. 9, 30</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. G. 2,
				113 al.</span></i> — 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Considered, on account of its poisonous
					berries, as a tree of the infernal regions,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. M.
					4, 432</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Sil. 13, 596</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Luc. 3,
			419</span></i>; <i><span class="en">6, 645
			al.</span></i>—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Poet.</b>, transf., <i>a
			javelin</i>, made of the wood of the yew-tree, <i><span class="en">Sil. 13,
				210</span></i>.</div>
